# Build-context allowlist for the containerized E2E harness
# (plans/containerized-harness-e2e.md, C6b rule 1 — a local-only working note,
# gitignored and absent from a fresh clone).
#
# `docker build` reads .dockerignore from the CONTEXT directory, never from
# beside the `-f` Dockerfile. The harness build is
#
#     docker build -f skills/multi-llm/tests/container/Dockerfile <repo-root>
#
# so the context is the repo root, this file has to live here, and every path
# below is repo-root-relative. A copy dropped under tests/container/ next to the
# Dockerfile is silently inert: the build would then upload the whole repo
# unfiltered while wearing a green build as a disguise.
#
# The file is allow-nothing-by-default. `*` puts everything out, and every
# runtime source the image needs is then negated back in by name -- which makes
# the allowlist a runtime manifest, because allow-nothing means the product
# under test is out too. It mirrors
# skills/multi-llm/tests/container/context_manifest.txt, and
# skills/multi-llm/tests/test_build_context.py builds the context from a clean
# `git worktree` checkout and asserts the two agree in both directions.
#
# Three semantics this file depends on, all measured rather than reasoned about:
#
#   1. COMMENTS MUST BE ON THEIR OWN LINE. Docker skips a line that *starts*
#      with `#`, but it does not strip a trailing comment: the plan's draft form
#      `!skills/multi-llm/*.py    # every orchestrator` is read as one pattern
#      containing spaces and a `#`, matches nothing, and silently drops every
#      .py from the context. Measured on this tree: that single line costs 17
#      files and the export still looks green.
#   2. A DIRECTORY PATH MATCHES THE DIRECTORY ENTRY, NOT ITS CONTENTS. The
#      tempting `!path/to/dir/` form copies an empty directory and nothing else,
#      so every directory allowlist below is written `/**`.
#   3. NO BARE PARENT NEGATION (`!skills`, `!skills/multi-llm`). The matcher
#      seeds each child's decision with its parent's, so one un-excluded parent
#      re-includes its entire subtree and silently converts this allowlist back
#      into a denylist.
#
# Rule 3 left open the question of whether a builder will descend into a
# directory that `*` excludes. FORM SHIPPED: no ancestor negations were needed.
# Verified by tests/test_build_context.py against BuildKit v0.24.0 / v0.31.1
# (Docker Engine 28.4.0, buildx 0.28.0) -- `skills/` is excluded by `*` and the
# skill still exports in full, because the builder descends whenever a negation
# pattern is prefixed by an excluded directory. The plan's bounded remedy
# (`!skills/` + `!skills/multi-llm/` + `!skills/multi-llm/tests/`, each
# immediately followed by a `skills/multi-llm/*` style re-exclusion placed above
# the leaf negations) is therefore NOT applied here. If a future builder does
# decline to descend, apply that remedy in full -- never a bare parent negation.

# Everything is out ...
*

# ... except the product under test.
# multi_llm.py, modes.py and every orchestrator:
!skills/multi-llm/*.py
!skills/multi-llm/providers.yaml
!skills/multi-llm/pyproject.toml
!skills/multi-llm/uv.lock
!skills/multi-llm/SKILL.md
!skills/multi-llm/utils/**
!skills/multi-llm/instructions/**
# the instruction core cites these at runtime:
!skills/multi-llm/references/**
!skills/multi-llm/prompts/**
!skills/multi-llm/schemas/**
!skills/multi-llm/templates/**
# inlined by the HTML report:
!skills/multi-llm/assets/icons/**
# capabilities.yaml + shim templates + snippets (host lane):
!skills/multi-llm/hosts/**

# ... and the rig that drives it.
!skills/multi-llm/tests/__init__.py
!skills/multi-llm/tests/conftest.py
!skills/multi-llm/tests/scenario_matcher.py
!skills/multi-llm/tests/harness/**
!skills/multi-llm/tests/mocks/**
!skills/multi-llm/tests/container/**
!skills/multi-llm/tests/fixtures/**
!skills/multi-llm/tests/golden/**
!skills/multi-llm/tests/test_container_*.py

# Re-excluded from inside the allowed trees. Last match wins, so these have to
# stay BELOW the negations above.
**/__pycache__/**
# raw evidence bundles; the sibling records/ (C10 provenance) stays in:
skills/multi-llm/tests/container/runs/**
# Credential shapes that would otherwise ride in on an allowlisted tree. These
# are the locations .gitignore anchors under C6b rule 3, restated here because
# the build context does not consult .gitignore -- an untracked scratch
# creds.json inside tests/container/ is exactly the leak this line stops.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/creds.json
**/creds/**
**/*.credentials.json
**/.codex/auth.json
**/.local/share/opencode/auth.json
# ... but the committed value-free seed templates the image actually needs stay
# in, for the same reason .gitignore negates them back: opencode's credential
# file is literally named auth.json, so the rules above would otherwise shadow
# the seed set. This must remain the LAST word on that tree.
!skills/multi-llm/tests/container/home_seed/**
